  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMSINH uses re+re^3/6+re^5/120 for |re|<=0.01, (1/EXP(-re)-EXP(-re))/2 below 20, and EXP(|re|+LN(cos(im)/2)) above 709",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMSINH(inumber) rejects pure-real inputs where EXP(|re|) overflows with #NUM!, and evaluates sinh(re) as re + re^3/6 + re^5/120 for |re| <= 0.01, (1/EXP(-re) - EXP(-re))/2 for 0.01 < |re| < 20, and signed EXP(|re|)/2 for |re| >= 20. Off-axis (im != 0), it checks |im| < 2^27 and for re > 709 or re < -708 evaluates EXP(|re| + LN(cos(im)/2)) and EXP(|re| + LN(sin(im)/2)) without abs(), returning #NUM! when cos(im) <= 0 or sin(im) <= 0. All 1,288 full-bank IMSINH rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imsinh.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (prefix_metadata row 131); 1,288/1,288 full-bank rows match.",
